                <h2>Community Guidelines</h2>
                <p>Our communities are spaces of safety, respect, and mutual support. We commit to:</p>
                <ul>
                    <li><strong>Confidentiality:</strong> What is shared stays in the group</li>
                    <li><strong>Respect:</strong> We honor each person's experience and perspective</li>
                    <li><strong>Non-judgment:</strong> All experiences are valid; no shame or stigma</li>
                    <li><strong>Safety:</strong> We don't tolerate discrimination or harmful behavior</li>
                    <li><strong>Peer support, not professional advice:</strong> We support each other but don't replace professional care</li>
                </ul>

                <h2>For Family Members</h2>
                <p>
                    Family members and caregivers are welcome in all our communities. We also offer resources specifically designed to support
                    those caring for someone with schizophrenia.
                </p>

                <h2>Need Immediate Support?</h2>
                <p>
                    If you or someone you know is in crisis, please reach out to emergency services or a mental health hotline:
                </p>
                <ul>
                    <li><strong>India Suicide Prevention Helpline:</strong> 1393 (toll-free)</li>
                    <li><strong>AMICA Helpline:</strong> 99 40 21 21 21</li>
                    <li><strong>Emergency:</strong> 100 or go to your nearest hospital</li>
                </ul>
